## Code & workflow conventions

- **Don't rewrite working code.** Read existing patterns first, then extend incrementally.
- **`game-core` stays pure** — no socket, no DB, no UI. State in, result out. Deterministic given a seed.
- **Tests:** follow the existing game-core test style and fixtures. Never regress an existing test. New logic ships with tests.
- **Plan first** for any non-trivial change: output a short plan + list of files to add/change, and wait for approval before mass-editing.
- **One feature branch per slice** (e.g. `feat/bot-engine`). Keep diffs minimal and reviewable.
- **Scope discipline:** implement only the slice asked for; don't pull in adjacent v3 features unprompted.
- **Language:** match existing code conventions (code/comments). User-facing copy is ijekavica.

## Status maintenance

When a feature slice is completed or scope changes, update `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`: move items between Done / Partial / Not-done, update the "in progress / next" marker, and bump the "Last updated" date. Keep it concise. If this hasn't been done by the end of a working session, do it before wrapping up.

## Implementation order (agreed)

Bot engine (PRD §36, §40, §42) → name generator (§39) → bot-backfill into live rooms (§38) → Quick Play + home/matching redesign (§37, §49).

- **Reconnect + persistence** (§7.8, §20–21) is a **gate that must land before Quick Play with real users** and before any quantitative validation. It may wait behind the bot work, but not past that point.
- **Single-player is cut** (v3.2) — do not build it.
- **Disconnect/abandon** needs only a small client-UI fix (~0.5d: render abandoned state + offline indicator); do not build the pause/vote ceremony.
